{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/seam.ts | sed -n '1,180p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// Test injection facility (Story 0, FC-0.6): one mechanism, two named\n     2\t// points, pattern from Epic 02's intake walk hook. Production code carries\n     3\t// the points as no-ops unless a test installs a hook:\n     4\t//   - \"post-commit-advance\": fired by the boundary advance after intake's\n     5\t//     commit flush, before the advance computes (TC-4.6's failure injection —\n     6\t//     an installed hook that throws stands in for an advance failure);\n     7\t//   - \"compact-write\": fired by compact between the sweep and the view-write\n     8\t//     transaction (TC-2.4's crash injection — a throwing hook proves the\n     9\t//     prior view survives an aborted write).\n    10\t// Tests reach the setters through test/fixtures/view-seam.ts (the one\n    11\t// directory sanctioned to import below the SDK surface); production code\n    12\t// only ever fires.\n    13\texport type ViewInjectionPoint = \"post-commit-advance\" | \"compact-write\";\n    14\t\n    15\texport type ViewInjectionHook = () => void;\n    16\t\n    17\tconst hooks: Record<ViewInjectionPoint, ViewInjectionHook | null> = {\n    18\t  \"post-commit-advance\": null,\n    19\t  \"compact-write\": null,\n    20\t};\n    21\t\n    22\texport function setViewInjectionHook(\n    23\t  point: ViewInjectionPoint,\n    24\t  hook: ViewInjectionHook | null,\n    25\t): void {\n    26\t  hooks[point] = hook;\n    27\t}\n    28\t\n    29\t// The production-side call: a no-op when nothing is installed. An installed\n    30\t// hook's throw propagates to the call site on purpose — that is the injected\n    31\t// failure the call site must survive.\n    32\texport function fireViewInjection(point: ViewInjectionPoint): void {\n    33\t  hooks[point]?.();\n    34\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
