e.name}\\\": percentage ${key} must be a non-negative number, got ${share}`;\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:62:  const sum = BAND_KEYS.reduce((total, key) => total + profile.percentages[key], 0);\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:64:    return `profile \\\"${profile.name}\\\": percentages must sum to 100, got ${sum}`;\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:69:// A complete, merged profile validates whole: positive lower bound, finite\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:71:// violated constraint and the profile (AC-2.3's vocabulary, applied at\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:73:export function validateProfile(profile: ViewProfile): void {\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:74:  const violation = profileViolation(profile);\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:93:        `profile \\\"${entry.name}\\\" is partial but overrides no built-in (unknown built-in override target); built-ins are ${BUILT_IN_PROFILES.map((p) => `\\\"${p.name}\\\"`).join(\\\", \\\")} — a new profile must carry lowerBound and all four percentages`,\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:144:// The one resolution path: built-ins, user profiles merged by name, every\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:145:// resolved profile validated, visibility and threshold defaulted and checked.\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:149:  const profiles: Record<string, ViewProfile> = {};\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:151:    profiles[builtIn.name] = builtIn;\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:153:  for (const entry of config?.profiles ?? []) {\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:155:      fail(`profile entries must carry a non-empty name`);\\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.