dfce2-5596-41b8-bb85-147f88812a5b\\\"}\\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:4032:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_delta\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"(sweep) — its gate requires confirming the Epic 02 requeue patch and the persisted ter\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"170b7ef7-652c-4e7c-84c0-f4f391dda968\\\"}\\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:4033:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_delta\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"minal-failure reason classes (FC-0.4 already proves the fixture side), and it flips the receipt's sweep field\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"120b4400-d6de-49a1-ab49-b5c563d392a1\\\"}\\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:4035:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-fable-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_01EWFNiizBQvcGUwZEmqR85c\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ready-for-verification\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"planSummary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Built compact inside-out per the story's build strategy: (1) render.ts gained the degrade ladders (smooth/detailed/brief resolvers), gap entries as last rung, §subject keys, [degraded: …]/[inter-turn note] markers, and band assembly; (2) select.ts is new — readSelectionInputs (record/forms reads with the canonical-corruption check in the reads, pre-transaction) plus the pure selectArrangement walk implementing rules 1–6 with pinned tie-breakers (≤ inclusion, newest-first, turn-boundary snap, straggler attachment, coverage edge); (3) snapshot.ts gained replaceViewSnapshot — one BEGIN IMMEDIATE doing delete-cascade, header+band insert, and boundary reset; (4) index.ts compact assembles validate → [sweep absent] → read → select → render → injection point → atomic replace → CompactReceipt with sweep: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Entry costs are tokens of the exact rendered entry text (one renderer, no drift). Two ambiguities surfaced during golden derivation and were pinned with code rationale: (a) turns whose chunk straddles the tail or is open are smooth-obligate and always render (AC-2.4's sanctioned over-bound indivisible-entry case — the alternative silently drops spans, violating TC-2.3); (b) a budget stop splitting a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk so it represents whole; (c) the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4's coverage edge is the documented exclusion path). Goldens G1–G4 were hand-derived from the rules against the fixture's deterministic token costs, verified against the pure walk, committed as JSON, and pinned in the immutability manifest.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"changedFiles\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"NEW: selection inputs read with pre-transaction corruption detection (CanonicalCorruptionError) + pure six-rule arrangement walk with coverage edge\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Band-entry side: degrade-ladder resolvers per band, gap entries, §keys, degraded/inter-turn-note markers, excerpt lines, band text assembly\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"replaceViewSnapshot: atomic BEGIN IMMEDIATE delete-cascade/insert/boundary-reset (AC-2.6)\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"compact real: profile/params validation as caller errors, corruption abort, compact-write injection point, receipt with sweep \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; stub removed\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Extracted profileViolation so construction (throw) and compact (caller-error result) share one rule set\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/shared/view.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CompactReceipt.sweep gains the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" literal (Story 3 debt comment referencing this story file); new ViewCompactParams (nested-partial params for field-wise band overrides, AC-2.2)\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/shared/errors.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Two additive caller-error codes: unknown_profile, invalid_view_config (no new classes)\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/sdk.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ThreadViewSurface.compact params type → ViewCompactParams; type re-exported\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/red-manifest.json\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Re-recorded: amended view-pull.test.ts, new test files, and the five golden JSONs pinned for immutability\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/goldens/README.md\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Golden inventory, immutability rule, GOLDEN_DUMP=1 regeneration instructions\\\\\\\" }\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"tests\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"added\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 rejections named (105 sum, non-positive bound, unknown profile), thread unchanged by read-back\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 built-in profile compact, bound+mix in receipt, sweep literal 'absent'\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1/AC-2.2 field-wise param override over a named profile, receipt profile null\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.2 actuals near shares with whole-entry deviations, zero provider calls, record hash unchanged\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.6 §chunk keys in brief/detailed, §turn keys in smooth\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk coverage edge: covered_from=13, exclusion reported, no phantom gaps\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk restart: fresh SDK pulls byte-identical snapshot\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.4 crash injection at compact-write: prior view serves, rerun lands, no partial rows\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.3 degraded compact: pending rendering → excerpt, failed brief summary → detailed-truncated, c2 gap with reason, full accounting, zero provider calls\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.5 completion leg: status view-health live (degraded=2, gaps=1, builtAt)\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 canonical corruption → state_corruption naming open turns, prior view serves, record unchanged\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 control: derived-only damage compacts\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.3 banded-subject edit + drain → band bytes hash-identical, rebuilt summary in record only\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.5 tail delete vanishes; banded delete leaves snapshot; status reflects record change\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G1 proportions vs committed JSON\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2a exact-fill inclusion (≤ rule)\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2b one-under exclusion, band stops\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G3 oversized loner represents alone\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G4 straggler rides following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"modified\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: sanctioned amendment — compact's not-implemented leg removed (operation is real); sweep/materialize stub assertions kept\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"removed\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"totalAfterStory\\\\\\\": 263,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\\\\\": 20\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"gatesRun\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pnpm run green-verify\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pnpm run verify-all\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\" }\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"selfReview\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"findingsFixed\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Initial literal reading of rules 2–4 silently dropped spans when the smooth budget stopped mid-chunk or a chunk straddled the tail (found by dumping the fixture: t4/t5 vanished under 25/25/25/25) — fixed with smooth-obligate always-include + partial-chunk retreat, both grounded in AC-2.4's indivisible-entry over-bound allowance and AC-2.5's never-omit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Compact-point walk had a malformed never-reached-budget branch — rewritten as explicit crossing detection\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Referential corruption check wrongly compared chunk members against live turns only — tombstoned turns are legitimate reference targets, now checked against all turn rows\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"receipt.profile initially named the base profile even when params overrode it — corrected to null whenever explicit params are present (tech design §Storage: 'null when explicit params')\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Pinned Partial<ViewProfile> params type could not express the single-band override AC-2.2 itself requires — deepened to ViewCompactParams (nested partial)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Golden authoring note: arrangements were hand-derived from the design rules using the fixture's deterministic token costs (dumped via a throwaway script, deleted), then the pure walk was checked against the hand derivation before committing — the goldens encode the rules, with regeneration instructions gated on the deviation process\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"view-pull.test.ts's skeleton test asserted compact returns not_implemented; amended under the established Epic 02 sanctioned-amendment precedent (cc304bb) and the manifest re-recorded\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ]\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"openQuestions\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Default base profile for a bare compact({}) is pinned to 'continuation' (first built-in, the epic's primary PI-continuation user); the design names no default — confirm or change the pin before the CLI (Story 5 surface) exposes it\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"specDeviations\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Pinned interpretation (not a behavior change to any stated rule): banded turns with no available chunk representation (chunk open or straddling the tail) always render in the smooth band even past its share — justified by AC-2.4's 'above it (an indivisible turn… included by the selection rules)' and required by AC-2.5/TC-2.3's no-silent-absence; documented in select.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Pinned interpretation: a budget stop that splits a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk (a chunk represents all of its members or none) — closes the straddle hole rule 3's 'entirely older' would otherwise leave\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Pinned interpretation: the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4 states the coverage edge, not 'same fill rule') — without this, the oldest chunk could never fall outside the window and the coverage-edge AC would be untestable\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"compact opts params type is ViewCompactParams (nested partial) rather than the sketched Partial<ViewProfile> — AC-2.2's field-wise band override is inexpressible in the sketched type\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Additive vocabulary: ErrorCode gains unknown_profile and invalid_view_config (caller_error class; no new classes per the error contract); CompactReceipt.sweep gains the 'absent' literal this story (Story 3 flips it, comment references this story file)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Run story verification; on acceptance proceed to Story 3 (sweep) — its gate requires confirming the Epic 02 requeue patch and the persisted terminal-failure reason classes (FC-0.4 already proves the fixture side), and it flips the receipt's sweep field from the 'absent' literal to SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }\\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":372,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":306568,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":372},\\\"output_tokens\\\":1,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\"},\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"8305205d-ae8a-4136-bc8c-6044d9b42470\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CbwmPnJirQE2KbPJrA1Ax\\\"}\\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:4039:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false,\\\"api_error_status\\\":null,\\\"duration_ms\\\":2324833,\\\"duration_api_ms\\\":2309337,\\\"ttft_ms\\\":3954,\\\"ttft_stream_ms\\\":3952,\\\"time_to_request_ms\\\":19,\\\"num_turns\\\":120,\\\"result\\\":\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ready-for-verification\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"planSummary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Built compact inside-out per the story's build strategy: (1) render.ts gained the degrade ladders (smooth/detailed/brief resolvers), gap entries as last rung, §subject keys, [degraded: …]/[inter-turn note] markers, and band assembly; (2) select.ts is new — readSelectionInputs (record/forms reads with the canonical-corruption check in the reads, pre-transaction) plus the pure selectArrangement walk implementing rules 1–6 with pinned tie-breakers (≤ inclusion, newest-first, turn-boundary snap, straggler attachment, coverage edge); (3) snapshot.ts gained replaceViewSnapshot — one BEGIN IMMEDIATE doing delete-cascade, header+band insert, and boundary reset; (4) index.ts compact assembles validate → [sweep absent] → read → select → render → injection point → atomic replace → CompactReceipt with sweep: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Entry costs are tokens of the exact rendered entry text (one renderer, no drift). Two ambiguities surfaced during golden derivation and were pinned with code rationale: (a) turns whose chunk straddles the tail or is open are smooth-obligate and always render (AC-2.4's sanctioned over-bound indivisible-entry case — the alternative silently drops spans, violating TC-2.3); (b) a budget stop splitting a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk so it represents whole; (c) the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4's coverage edge is the documented exclusion path). Goldens G1–G4 were hand-derived from the rules against the fixture's deterministic token costs, verified against the pure walk, committed as JSON, and pinned in the immutability manifest.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"changedFiles\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"NEW: selection inputs read with pre-transaction corruption detection (CanonicalCorruptionError) + pure six-rule arrangement walk with coverage edge\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Band-entry side: degrade-ladder resolvers per band, gap entries, §keys, degraded/inter-turn-note markers, excerpt lines, band text assembly\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"replaceViewSnapshot: atomic BEGIN IMMEDIATE delete-cascade/insert/boundary-reset (AC-2.6)\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"compact real: profile/params validation as caller errors, corruption abort, compact-write injection point, receipt with sweep \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; stub removed\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Extracted profileViolation so construction (throw) and compact (caller-error result) share one rule set\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/shared/view.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CompactReceipt.sweep gains the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" literal (Story 3 debt comment referencing this story file); new ViewCompactParams (nested-partial params for field-wise band overrides, AC-2.2)\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/shared/errors.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Two additive caller-error codes: unknown_profile, invalid_view_config (no new classes)\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"src/sdk.ts\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ThreadViewSurface.compact params type → ViewCompactParams; type re-exported\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/red-manifest.json\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Re-recorded: amended view-pull.test.ts, new test files, and the five golden JSONs pinned for immutability\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/goldens/README.md\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reason\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Golden inventory, immutability rule, GOLDEN_DUMP=1 regeneration instructions\\\\\\\" }\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"tests\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"added\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 rejections named (105 sum, non-positive bound, unknown profile), thread unchanged by read-back\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 built-in profile compact, bound+mix in receipt, sweep literal 'absent'\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1/AC-2.2 field-wise param override over a named profile, receipt profile null\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.2 actuals near shares with whole-entry deviations, zero provider calls, record hash unchanged\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.6 §chunk keys in brief/detailed, §turn keys in smooth\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk coverage edge: covered_from=13, exclusion reported, no phantom gaps\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk restart: fresh SDK pulls byte-identical snapshot\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.4 crash injection at compact-write: prior view serves, rerun lands, no partial rows\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.3 degraded compact: pending rendering → excerpt, failed brief summary → detailed-truncated, c2 gap with reason, full accounting, zero provider calls\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.5 completion leg: status view-health live (degraded=2, gaps=1, builtAt)\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 canonical corruption → state_corruption naming open turns, prior view serves, record unchanged\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 control: derived-only damage compacts\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.3 banded-subject edit + drain → band bytes hash-identical, rebuilt summary in record only\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.5 tail delete vanishes; banded delete leaves snapshot; status reflects record change\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G1 proportions vs committed JSON\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2a exact-fill inclusion (≤ rule)\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2b one-under exclusion, band stops\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G3 oversized loner represents alone\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G4 straggler rides following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"modified\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: sanctioned amendment — compact's not-implemented leg removed (operation is real); sweep/materialize stub assertions kept\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"removed\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"totalAfterStory\\\\\\\": 263,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\\\\\": 20\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"gatesRun\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pnpm run green-verify\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\" },\\\\n    { \\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pnpm run verify-all\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\" }\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"selfReview\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"findingsFixed\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Initial literal reading of rules 2–4 silently dropped spans when the smooth budget stopped mid-chunk or a chunk straddled the tail (found by dumping the fixture: t4/t5 vanished under 25/25/25/25) — fixed with smooth-obligate always-include + partial-chunk retreat, both grounded in AC-2.4's indivisible-entry over-bound allowance and AC-2.5's never-omit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Compact-point walk had a malformed never-reached-budget branch — rewritten as explicit crossing detection\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Referential corruption check wrongly compared chunk members against live turns only — tombstoned turns are legitimate reference targets, now checked against all turn rows\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"receipt.profile initially named the base profile even when params overrode it — corrected to null whenever explicit params are present (tech design §Storage: 'null when explicit params')\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Pinned Partial<ViewProfile> params type could not express the single-band override AC-2.2 itself requires — deepened to ViewCompactParams (nested partial)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\\\\\": [\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Golden authoring note: arrangements were hand-derived from the design rules using the fixture's deterministic token costs (dumped via a throwaway script, deleted), then the pure walk was checked against the hand derivation before committing — the goldens encode the rules, with regeneration instructions gated on the deviation process\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"view-pull.test.ts's skeleton test asserted compact returns not_implemented; amended under the established Epic 02 sanctioned-amendment precedent (cc304bb) and the manifest re-recorded\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ]\\\\n  },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"openQuestions\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Default base profile for a bare compact({}) is pinned to 'continuation' (first built-in, the epic's primary PI-continuation user); the design names no default — confirm or change the pin before the CLI (Story 5 surface) exposes it\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"specDeviations\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Pinned interpretation (not a behavior change to any stated rule): banded turns with no available chunk representation (chunk open or straddling the tail) always render in the smooth band even past its share — justified by AC-2.4's 'above it (an indivisible turn… included by the selection rules)' and required by AC-2.5/TC-2.3's no-silent-absence; documented in select.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Pinned interpretation: a budget stop that splits a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk (a chunk represents all of its members or none) — closes the straddle hole rule 3's 'entirely older' would otherwise leave\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Pinned interpretation: the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4 states the coverage edge, not 'same fill rule') — without this, the oldest chunk could never fall outside the window and the coverage-edge AC would be untestable\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"compact opts params type is ViewCompactParams (nested partial) rather than the sketched Partial<ViewProfile> — AC-2.2's field-wise band override is inexpressible in the sketched type\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"Additive vocabulary: ErrorCode gains unknown_profile and invalid_view_config (caller_error class; no new classes per the error contract); CompactReceipt.sweep gains the 'absent' literal this story (Story 3 flips it, comment references this story file)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Run story verification; on acceptance proceed to Story 3 (sweep) — its gate requires confirming the Epic 02 requeue patch and the persisted terminal-failure reason classes (FC-0.4 already proves the fixture side), and it flips the receipt's sweep field from the 'absent' literal to SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }\\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":35.719216,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":11069,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":428027,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":19616208,\\\"output_tokens\\\":132397,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":428027,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"output_tokens\\\":3730,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":306568,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":372,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":372},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":1533,\\\"outputTokens\\\":17,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":0.001618,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000},\\\"claude-fable-5\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":11071,\\\"outputTokens\\\":145527,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":19769998,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":428027,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":35.717598,\\\"contextWindow\\\":1000000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":64000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"86902755-a8cb-41e1-bc8b-a1bb42edb4ec\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts | sed -n '1,520p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// Band selection (Story 2): the six-rule walk from tech design §Deterministic\\n     2\\t// Algorithms — compact point, smooth/detailed/brief fills, rule-5 unchunked\\n     3\\t// turns, rule-6 turnless stragglers — plus the coverage edge (covered_from)\\n     4\\t// and canonical-corruption detection. Two halves, deliberately split:\\n     5\\t//\\n     6\\t//   - readSelectionInputs: the record/forms reads, with the corruption check\\n     7\\t//     IN the reads, before any transaction opens (story Technical Notes) —\\n     8\\t//     a refusal here means nothing was written, so the prior view is\\n     9\\t//     trivially intact (AC-2.5). Never moved inside the transaction.\\n    10\\t//   - selectArrangement: a pure function over those inputs. No DB handle, no\\n    11\\t//     clock, no provider — same inputs ⇒ same arrangement, byte-for-byte\\n    12\\t//     (AC-2.9; goldens G1–G4 pin the tie-breakers).\\n    13\\t//\\n    14\\t// Tie-breakers, pinned (tech design): inclusion thresholds are ≤; walks are\\n    15\\t// newest-first everywhere; chunk coverage is decided by the chunk's newest\\n    16\\t// member turn. Entry costs are the tokens of the rendered entry text itself\\n    17\\t// (render.ts's renderArrangementEntry, including attached inter-turn notes),\\n    18\\t// so the budgeted tokens are the stored tokens — no second estimate.\\n    19\\timport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n    20\\timport { estimateTokens } from \\\"../../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\n    21\\timport type { Band } from \\\"../../../shared/view.js\\\";\\n    22\\timport {\\n    23\\t  excerptLine,\\n    24\\t  renderArrangementEntry,\\n    25\\t  resolveBriefRepresentation,\\n    26\\t  resolveDetailedRepresentation,\\n    27\\t  resolveSmoothRepresentation,\\n    28\\t  type FormSnapshot,\\n    29\\t} from \\\"./render.js\\\";\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t// Canonical source state needed to identify or read the compacted span is\\n    32\\t// damaged: compact refuses with state_corruption (AC-2.5). Derived-material\\n    33\\t// damage never raises this — it degrades through the ladders instead.\\n    34\\texport class CanonicalCorruptionError extends Error {\\n    35\\t  readonly code: \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\" | \\\"source_damaged\\\";\\n    36\\t  constructor(code: \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\" | \\\"source_damaged\\\", reason: string) {\\n    37\\t    super(reason);\\n    38\\t    this.code = code;\\n    39\\t    this.name = \\\"CanonicalCorruptionError\\\";\\n    40\\t  }\\n    41\\t}\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\texport interface SelectionMessage {\\n    44\\t  messageId: string;\\n    45\\t  order: number; // source_event_order\\n    46\\t  kind: string;\\n    47\\t  tokenEstimate: number;\\n    48\\t  turnId: string | null;\\n    49\\t  text: string; // excerpt/note line (render.excerptLine)\\n    50\\t}\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\texport interface SelectionTurn {\\n    53\\t  turnId: string;\\n    54\\t  turnOrder: number;\\n    55\\t  status: \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\";\\n    56\\t  openedAt: number;\\n    57\\t  closedAt: number | null;\\n    58\\t}\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\texport interface SelectionChunk {\\n    61\\t  chunkId: string;\\n    62\\t  chunkOrder: number;\\n    63\\t  status: \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\";\\n    64\\t  memberTurnIds: string[]; // member order\\n    65\\t}\\n    66\\t\\n    67\\texport interface SelectionInputs {\\n    68\\t  messages: SelectionMessage[]; // live only, ascending order\\n    69\\t  turns: SelectionTurn[]; // ascending turnOrder\\n    70\\t  chunks: SelectionChunk[]; // ascending chunkOrder\\n    71\\t  forms: Map<string, FormSnapshot>; // `${subjectId}/${form}` (turn/chunk subjects)\\n    72\\t  maxEventOrder: number;\\n    73\\t  formCounts: Record<string, Record<string, number>>; // form → state → count\\n    74\\t}\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\texport interface ArrangementEntry {\\n    77\\t  band: Band;\\n    78\\t  subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n    79\\t  subjectId: string;\\n    80\\t  formUsed: string;\\n    81\\t  degraded: boolean;\\n    82\\t  gap: boolean;\\n    83\\t  reason?: string; // gap entries\\n    84\\t  startOrder: number; // oldest event order the entry represents (notes included)\\n    85\\t  text: string; // rendered entry text (the band stores this verbatim)\\n    86\\t  tokens: number;\\n    87\\t}\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\texport interface SelectionResult {\\n    90\\t  compactPoint: number;\\n    91\\t  coveredFrom: number;\\n    92\\t  // Gradient order (brief → detailed → smooth), oldest-first within band —\\n    93\\t  // the order the bands render and the arrangement persists.\\n    94\\t  entries: ArrangementEntry[];\\n    95\\t}\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t// ── reads (corruption check lives here, pre-transaction) ─────────\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\texport function readSelectionInputs(db: DatabaseSync): SelectionInputs {\\n   100\\t  const turnRows = db\\n   101\\t    .prepare(\\n   102\\t      `SELECT turn_id, turn_order, status, opened_at_event_order, closed_at_event_order, deleted_at\\n   103\\t       FROM turns ORDER BY turn_order`,\\n   104\\t    )\\n   105\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{\\n   106\\t    turn_id: string;\\n   107\\t    turn_order: number | bigint;\\n   108\\t    status: string;\\n   109\\t    opened_at_event_order: number | bigint;\\n   110\\t    closed_at_event_order: number | bigint | null;\\n   111\\t    deleted_at: string | null;\\n   112\\t  }>;\\n   113\\t  // Referential checks compare against every turn row (a tombstoned turn is\\n   114\\t  // a legitimate reference target, not damage); the selection walk itself\\n   115\\t  // sees live turns only.\\n   116\\t  const turnIds = new Set(turnRows.map((row) => row.turn_id));\\n   117\\t  const turns: SelectionTurn[] = turnRows\\n   118\\t    .filter((row) => row.deleted_at === null)\\n   119\\t    .map((row) => ({\\n   120\\t      turnId: row.turn_id,\\n   121\\t      turnOrder: Number(row.turn_order),\\n   122\\t      status: row.status as \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\",\\n   123\\t      openedAt: Number(row.opened_at_event_order),\\n   124\\t      closedAt: row.closed_at_event_order === null ? null : Number(row.closed_at_event_order),\\n   125\\t    }));\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  // Canonical damage the walk cannot select across (AC-2.5): the Epic 01\\n   128\\t  // turn-state invariant (at most one open turn, open turns carry no close),\\n   129\\t  // and referential damage between the chunk/message rows and their turns.\\n   130\\t  const openTurns = turns.filter((turn) => turn.status === \\\"open\\\");\\n   131\\t  if (openTurns.length > 1) {\\n   132\\t    throw new CanonicalCorruptionError(\\n   133\\t      \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\",\\n   134\\t      `canonical turn state corrupt: ${openTurns.length} open turns (${openTurns\\n   135\\t        .map((turn) => turn.turnId)\\n   136\\t        .join(\\\", \\\")}); the compacted span cannot be identified`,\\n   137\\t    );\\n   138\\t  }\\n   139\\t  for (const turn of turns) {\\n   140\\t    if (turn.status === \\\"closed\\\" && turn.closedAt === null) {\\n   141\\t      throw new CanonicalCorruptionError(\\n   142\\t        \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n   143\\t        `canonical turn state corrupt: closed turn ${turn.turnId} carries no close boundary`,\\n   144\\t      );\\n   145\\t    }\\n   146\\t  }\\n   147\\t\\n   148\\t  const messageRows = db\\n   149\\t    .prepare(\\n   150\\t      `SELECT message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, turn_id\\n   151\\t       FROM message WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY source_event_order`,\\n   152\\t    )\\n   153\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{\\n   154\\t    message_id: string;\\n   155\\t    source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n   156\\t    kind: string;\\n   157\\t    token_estimate: number | bigint;\\n   158\\t    turn_id: string | null;\\n   159\\t  }>;\\n   160\\t  const blockRows = db\\n   161\\t    .prepare(\\n   162\\t      `SELECT mb.message_id, mb.block_type, mb.content\\n   163\\t       FROM message_block mb JOIN message m ON m.message_id = mb.message_id\\n   164\\t       WHERE m.deleted_at IS NULL\\n   165\\t       ORDER BY m.source_event_order, mb.block_index`,\\n   166\\t    )\\n   167\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{ message_id: string; block_type: string; content: string }>;\\n   168\\t  const blocksByMessage = new Map<\\n   169\\t    string,\\n   170\\t    Array<{ blockType: string; content: Record<string, unknown> }>\\n   171\\t  >();\\n   172\\t  for (const row of blockRows) {\\n   173\\t    const blocks = blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? [];\\n   174\\t    blocks.push({\\n   175\\t      blockType: row.block_type,\\n   176\\t      content: JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n   177\\t    });\\n   178\\t    blocksByMessage.set(row.message_id, blocks);\\n   179\\t  }\\n   180\\t  const messages: SelectionMessage[] = messageRows.map((row) => {\\n   181\\t    if (row.turn_id !== null && !turnIds.has(row.turn_id)) {\\n   182\\t      throw new CanonicalCorruptionError(\\n   183\\t        \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n   184\\t        `canonical record corrupt: message ${row.message_id} references missing turn ${row.turn_id}`,\\n   185\\t      );\\n   186\\t    }\\n   187\\t    return {\\n   188\\t      messageId: row.message_id,\\n   189\\t      order: Number(row.source_event_order),\\n   190\\t      kind: row.kind,\\n   191\\t      tokenEstimate: Number(row.token_estimate),\\n   192\\t      turnId: row.turn_id,\\n   193\\t      text: excerptLine(row.kind, blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? []),\\n   194\\t    };\\n   195\\t  });\\n   196\\t\\n   197\\t  const chunkRows = db\\n   198\\t    .prepare(`SELECT chunk_id, chunk_order, status FROM chunk ORDER BY chunk_order`)\\n   199\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{ chunk_id: string; chunk_order: number | bigint; status: string }>;\\n   200\\t  const memberRows = db\\n   201\\t    .prepare(\\n   202\\t      `SELECT cm.chunk_id, cm.turn_id, cm.member_idx FROM chunk_member cm\\n   203\\t       JOIN chunk c ON c.chunk_id = cm.chunk_id\\n   204\\t       ORDER BY c.chunk_order, cm.member_idx`,\\n   205\\t    )\\n   206\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{ chunk_id: string; turn_id: string; member_idx: number | bigint }>;\\n   207\\t  const membersByChunk = new Map<string, string[]>();\\n   208\\t  for (const row of memberRows) {\\n   209\\t    if (!turnIds.has(row.turn_id)) {\\n   210\\t      throw new CanonicalCorruptionError(\\n   211\\t        \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n   212\\t        `canonical record corrupt: chunk ${row.chunk_id} membership references missing turn ${row.turn_id}`,\\n   213\\t      );\\n   214\\t    }\\n   215\\t    const members = membersByChunk.get(row.chunk_id) ?? [];\\n   216\\t    members.push(row.turn_id);\\n   217\\t    membersByChunk.set(row.chunk_id, members);\\n   218\\t  }\\n   219\\t  const chunks: SelectionChunk[] = chunkRows.map((row) => ({\\n   220\\t    chunkId: row.chunk_id,\\n   221\\t    chunkOrder: Number(row.chunk_order),\\n   222\\t    status: row.status as \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\",\\n   223\\t    memberTurnIds: membersByChunk.get(row.chunk_id) ?? [],\\n   224\\t  }));\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t  const formRows = db\\n   227\\t    .prepare(\\n   228\\t      `SELECT subject_id, form, state, content, reason FROM derived_form\\n   229\\t       WHERE subject_kind IN ('turn', 'chunk')`,\\n   230\\t    )\\n   231\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{\\n   232\\t    subject_id: string;\\n   233\\t    form: string;\\n   234\\t    state: string;\\n   235\\t    content: string | null;\\n   236\\t    reason: string | null;\\n   237\\t  }>;\\n   238\\t  const forms = new Map<string, FormSnapshot>();\\n   239\\t  for (const row of formRows) {\\n   240\\t    const snapshot: FormSnapshot = { state: row.state as FormSnapshot[\\\"state\\\"] };\\n   241\\t    if (row.content !== null) snapshot.content = row.content;\\n   242\\t    if (row.reason !== null) snapshot.reason = row.reason;\\n   243\\t    forms.set(`${row.subject_id}/${row.form}`, snapshot);\\n   244\\t  }\\n   245\\t\\n   246\\t  const maxRow = db.prepare(`SELECT COALESCE(MAX(event_order), 0) AS m FROM event`).get() as {\\n   247\\t    m: number | bigint;\\n   248\\t  };\\n   249\\t  const countRows = db\\n   250\\t    .prepare(`SELECT form, state, COUNT(*) AS n FROM derived_form GROUP BY form, state`)\\n   251\\t    .all() as unknown as Array<{ form: string; state: string; n: number | bigint }>;\\n   252\\t  const formCounts: Record<string, Record<string, number>> = {};\\n   253\\t  for (const row of countRows) {\\n   254\\t    formCounts[row.form] = { ...formCounts[row.form], [row.state]: Number(row.n) };\\n   255\\t  }\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\t  return { messages, turns, chunks, forms, maxEventOrder: Number(maxRow.m), formCounts };\\n   258\\t}\\n   259\\t\\n   260\\t// ── the pure walk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n   261\\t\\n   262\\texport interface SelectionConfig {\\n   263\\t  lowerBound: number;\\n   264\\t  percentages: { full: number; smooth: number; detailed: number; brief: number };\\n   265\\t}\\n   266\\t\\n   267\\texport function selectArrangement(\\n   268\\t  inputs: SelectionInputs,\\n   269\\t  config: SelectionConfig,\\n   270\\t): SelectionResult {\\n   271\\t  const { messages, turns, chunks, forms } = inputs;\\n   272\\t  const lookup = (subjectId: string, form: string): FormSnapshot | undefined =>\\n   273\\t    forms.get(`${subjectId}/${form}`);\\n   274\\t  const budget = (share: number): number => (config.lowerBound * share) / 100;\\n   275\\t\\n   276\\t  const turnsById = new Map(turns.map((turn) => [turn.turnId, turn]));\\n   277\\t  const messagesByTurn = new Map<string, SelectionMessage[]>();\\n   278\\t  for (const message of messages) {\\n   279\\t    if (message.turnId === null) continue;\\n   280\\t    const list = messagesByTurn.get(message.turnId) ?? [];\\n   281\\t    list.push(message);\\n   282\\t    messagesByTurn.set(message.turnId, list);\\n   283\\t  }\\n   284\\t\\n   285\\t  // Rule 6: turnless stragglers attach to the FOLLOWING turn — they ride its\\n   286\\t  // band assignment, price into its fill cost, and render marked immediately\\n   287\\t  // before its entry. No following turn ⇒ tail by construction.\\n   288\\t  const notesByTurn = new Map<string, SelectionMessage[]>();\\n   289\\t  for (const message of messages) {\\n   290\\t    if (message.turnId !== null) continue;\\n   291\\t    const following = turns.find((turn) => turn.openedAt > message.order);\\n   292\\t    if (following === undefined) continue; // trailing straggler: tail\\n   293\\t    const list = notesByTurn.get(following.turnId) ?? [];\\n   294\\t    list.push(message);\\n   295\\t    notesByTurn.set(following.turnId, list);\\n   296\\t  }\\n   297\\t\\n   298\\t  // The oldest event order a turn's entry represents: its oldest live\\n   299\\t  // message or attached note, falling back to its open boundary.\\n   300\\t  function turnStartOrder(turn: SelectionTurn): number {\\n   301\\t    const candidates = [\\n   302\\t      ...(messagesByTurn.get(turn.turnId) ?? []).map((message) => message.order),\\n   303\\t      ...(notesByTurn.get(turn.turnId) ?? []).map((note) => note.order),\\n   304\\t    ];\\n   305\\t    return candidates.length === 0 ? turn.openedAt : Math.min(...candidates);\\n   306\\t  }\\n   307\\t\\n   308\\t  // Rule 1 — compact point: messages newest-first until the estimate sum\\n   309\\t  // first reaches the full share; the point snaps to a turn boundary so the\\n   310\\t  // tail never begins mid-turn. Open-turn messages always land in the tail.\\n   311\\t  const fullBudget = budget(config.percentages.full);\\n   312\\t  const closedTurns = turns.filter((turn) => turn.status === \\\"closed\\\");\\n   313\\t  let compactPoint = 0;\\n   314\\t  if (closedTurns.length > 0 && messages.length > 0) {\\n   315\\t    let sum = 0;\\n   316\\t    let crossing: SelectionMessage | null = null;\\n   317\\t    for (let i = messages.length - 1; i >= 0; i -= 1) {\\n   318\\t      const message = messages[i] as SelectionMessage;\\n   319\\t      sum += message.tokenEstimate;\\n   320\\t      if (sum >= fullBudget) {\\n   321\\t        crossing = message;\\n   322\\t        break;\\n   323\\t      }\\n   324\\t    }\\n   325\\t    // Budget never reached ⇒ the whole record fits the full share:\\n   326\\t    // everything is tail, no bands.\\n   327\\t    compactPoint = crossing === null ? 0 : snapCompactPoint(crossing);\\n   328\\t  }\\n   329\\t\\n   330\\t  function snapCompactPoint(oldestTaken: SelectionMessage): number {\\n   331\\t    // The turn whose boundary the point snaps against: the message's own\\n   332\\t    // turn, or — for a turnless straggler — the turn it attaches to.\\n   333\\t    let candidate: SelectionTurn | undefined =\\n   334\\t      oldestTaken.turnId !== null ? turnsById.get(oldestTaken.turnId) : undefined;\\n   335\\t    if (candidate === undefined && oldestTaken.turnId === null) {\\n   336\\t      candidate = turns.find((turn) => turn.openedAt > oldestTaken.order);\\n   337\\t    }\\n   338\\t    const previousClose = (turn: SelectionTurn): number => {\\n   339\\t      const previous = closedTurns.filter((t) => t.turnOrder < turn.turnOrder).at(-1);\\n   340\\t      return previous?.closedAt ?? 0;\\n   341\\t    };\\n   342\\t    if (candidate === undefined) {\\n   343\\t      // A trailing straggler with no following turn sits after the last turn\\n   344\\t      // boundary, where the compact point cannot pass it: tail begins after\\n   345\\t      // the newest closed turn.\\n   346\\t      return closedTurns.at(-1)?.closedAt ?? 0;\\n   347\\t    }\\n   348\\t    if (candidate.status === \\\"open\\\") {\\n   349\\t      // Open-turn messages are tail regardless of budget; the tail begins at\\n   350\\t      // the open turn's start.\\n   351\\t      return previousClose(candidate);\\n   352\\t    }\\n   353\\t    // Fully covered down to the turn's start (notes included) ⇒ the tail\\n   354\\t    // begins at this turn; otherwise snap FORWARD to the next turn start —\\n   355\\t    // the partially-covered turn falls whole to the bands.\\n   356\\t    if (oldestTaken.order <= turnStartOrder(candidate)) {\\n   357\\t      return previousClose(candidate);\\n   358\\t    }\\n   359\\t    return candidate.closedAt ?? 0;\\n   360\\t  }\\n   361\\t\\n   362\\t  // Band candidates: closed turns wholly behind the compact point. Rule 5 is\\n   363\\t  // structural here — chunked or not, a banded turn is a smooth candidate\\n   364\\t  // (bands are defined by representation, not strict time strata).\\n   365\\t  const bandedTurns = closedTurns.filter(\\n   366\\t    (turn) => turn.closedAt !== null && turn.closedAt <= compactPoint,\\n   367\\t  );\\n   368\\t  const bandedTurnIds = new Set(bandedTurns.map((turn) => turn.turnId));\\n   369\\t\\n   370\\t  function buildTurnEntry(turn: SelectionTurn): ArrangementEntry {\\n   371\\t    const turnMessages = messagesByTurn.get(turn.turnId) ?? [];\\n   372\\t    const excerpt =\\n   373\\t      turnMessages.length === 0 ? null : turnMessages.map((message) => message.text).join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n   374\\t    const rep = resolveSmoothRepresentation(turn.turnId, lookup, excerpt);\\n   375\\t    const noteTexts = (notesByTurn.get(turn.turnId) ?? []).map((note) => note.text);\\n   376\\t    const text = renderArrangementEntry(\\\"turn\\\", turn.turnId, rep, noteTexts);\\n   377\\t    const entry: ArrangementEntry = {\\n   378\\t      band: \\\"smooth\\\",\\n   379\\t      subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\",\\n   380\\t      subjectId: turn.turnId,\\n   381\\t      formUsed: rep.formUsed,\\n   382\\t      degraded: rep.degraded,\\n   383\\t      gap: rep.gap,\\n   384\\t      startOrder: turnStartOrder(turn),\\n   385\\t      text,\\n   386\\t      tokens: estimateTokens(text),\\n   387\\t    };\\n   388\\t    if (rep.reason !== undefined) entry.reason = rep.reason;\\n   389\\t    return entry;\\n   390\\t  }\\n   391\\t\\n   392\\t  function buildChunkEntry(chunk: SelectionChunk, band: \\\"detailed\\\" | \\\"brief\\\"): ArrangementEntry {\\n   393\\t    const memberProjections = chunk.memberTurnIds\\n   394\\t      .map((turnId) => lookup(turnId, \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"))\\n   395\\t      .filter((form): form is FormSnapshot & { content: string } => form?.state === \\\"ready\\\")\\n   396\\t      .map((form) => form.content ?? \\\"\\\")\\n   397\\t      .filter((content) => content.length > 0);\\n   398\\t    const rep =\\n   399\\t      band === \\\"detailed\\\"\\n   400\\t        ? resolveDetailedRepresentation(chunk.chunkId, lookup, memberProjections)\\n   401\\t        : resolveBriefRepresentation(chunk.chunkId, lookup);\\n   402\\t    const noteTexts = chunk.memberTurnIds.flatMap((turnId) =>\\n   403\\t      (notesByTurn.get(turnId) ?? []).map((note) => note.text),\\n   404\\t    );\\n   405\\t    const text = renderArrangementEntry(\\\"chunk\\\", chunk.chunkId, rep, noteTexts);\\n   406\\t    const memberStarts = chunk.memberTurnIds\\n   407\\t      .map((turnId) => turnsById.get(turnId))\\n   408\\t      .filter((turn): turn is SelectionTurn => turn !== undefined)\\n   409\\t      .map((turn) => turnStartOrder(turn));\\n   410\\t    const entry: ArrangementEntry = {\\n   411\\t      band,\\n   412\\t      subjectKind: \\\"chunk\\\",\\n   413\\t      subjectId: chunk.chunkId,\\n   414\\t      formUsed: rep.formUsed,\\n   415\\t      degraded: rep.degraded,\\n   416\\t      gap: rep.gap,\\n   417\\t      startOrder: memberStarts.length === 0 ? compactPoint : Math.min(...memberStarts),\\n   418\\t      text,\\n   419\\t      tokens: estimateTokens(text),\\n   420\\t    };\\n   421\\t    if (rep.reason !== undefined) entry.reason = rep.reason;\\n   422\\t    return entry;\\n   423\\t  }\\n   424\\t\\n   425\\t  // Chunk representation is available to a turn only through a closed chunk\\n   426\\t  // whose live members ALL sit behind the compact point — a chunk straddling\\n   427\\t  // the tail (or still open) cannot stand in for its banded members. Such\\n   428\\t  // members are smooth-obligate: the smooth band is their only\\n   429\\t  // representation, so the walk always includes them — this is AC-2.4's\\n   430\\t  // sanctioned over-bound case (\\\"an indivisible turn … included by the\\n   431\\t  // selection rules\\\") and what keeps every span in the compacted range\\n   432\\t  // accounted for (AC-2.5, TC-2.3's no-silent-absence).\\n   433\\t  const liveMembersOf = (chunk: SelectionChunk): SelectionTurn[] =>\\n   434\\t    chunk.memberTurnIds\\n   435\\t      .map((turnId) => turnsById.get(turnId))\\n   436\\t      .filter((turn): turn is SelectionTurn => turn !== undefined);\\n   437\\t  const fullyBandedChunks = chunks.filter((chunk) => {\\n   438\\t    const members = liveMembersOf(chunk);\\n   439\\t    return (\\n   440\\t      chunk.status === \\\"closed\\\" &&\\n   441\\t      members.length > 0 &&\\n   442\\t      members.every((turn) => bandedTurnIds.has(turn.turnId))\\n   443\\t    );\\n   444\\t  });\\n   445\\t  const chunkRepresentableTurnIds = new Set(\\n   446\\t    fullyBandedChunks.flatMap((chunk) => chunk.memberTurnIds),\\n   447\\t  );\\n   448\\t\\n   449\\t  // Rule 2 + 5 — smooth band: banded closed turns, newest-first (chunked or\\n   450\\t  // not — rule 5 is structural). Obligates always include; chunk-representable\\n   451\\t  // turns fill against the share with ≤ inclusion, and the first crossing one\\n   452\\t  // stops admission — the remainder takes chunk representation.\\n   453\\t  const smoothBudget = budget(config.percentages.smooth);\\n   454\\t  const smoothIncluded: ArrangementEntry[] = [];\\n   455\\t  let smoothSum = 0;\\n   456\\t  let smoothStopped = false;\\n   457\\t  for (const turn of [...bandedTurns].reverse()) {\\n   458\\t    const entry = buildTurnEntry(turn);\\n   459\\t    if (!chunkRepresentableTurnIds.has(turn.turnId)) {\\n   460\\t      smoothIncluded.push(entry);\\n   461\\t      smoothSum += entry.tokens;\\n   462\\t      continue;\\n   463\\t    }\\n   464\\t    if (smoothStopped) continue;\\n   465\\t    if (smoothSum + entry.tokens <= smoothBudget) {\\n   466\\t      smoothIncluded.push(entry);\\n   467\\t      smoothSum += entry.tokens;\\n   468\\t      continue;\\n   469\\t    }\\n   470\\t    if (smoothIncluded.length === 0) {\\n   471\\t      // Oversized loner on an otherwise-empty band: one turn still represents.\\n   472\\t      smoothIncluded.push(entry);\\n   473\\t    }\\n   474\\t    smoothStopped = true;\\n   475\\t  }\\n   476\\t\\n   477\\t  // Partial-chunk retreat: when the budget stop (or the loner rule) leaves a\\n   478\\t  // fully-banded chunk split — some members in the smooth band, some not —\\n   479\\t  // the included members retreat to the chunk, which then represents whole in\\n   480\\t  // a chunk band. Bands are defined by representation; a chunk can stand in\\n   481\\t  // for all of its members or none, never a slice (the alternative leaves the\\n   482\\t  // unincluded slice represented nowhere).\\n   483\\t  const smoothTurnIdSet = (): Set<string> =>\\n   484\\t    new Set(smoothIncluded.map((entry) => entry.subjectId));\\n   485\\t  for (const chunk of fullyBandedChunks) {\\n   486\\t    const inSmooth = smoothTurnIdSet();\\n   487\\t    const members = liveMembersOf(chunk);\\n   488\\t    const includedMembers = members.filter((turn) => inSmooth.has(turn.turnId));\\n   489\\t    if (includedMembers.length > 0 && includedMembers.length < members.length) {\\n   490\\t      const retreatIds = new Set(includedMembers.map((turn) => turn.turnId));\\n   491\\t      for (let i = smoothIncluded.length - 1; i >= 0; i -= 1) {\\n   492\\t        const entry = smoothIncluded[i] as ArrangementEntry;\\n   493\\t        if (retreatIds.has(entry.subjectId)) smoothIncluded.splice(i, 1);\\n   494\\t      }\\n   495\\t    }\\n   496\\t  }\\n   497\\t  const smoothTurnIds = smoothTurnIdSet();\\n   498\\t\\n   499\\t  // Rules 3–4 — chunk candidacy: fully banded, nothing already represented\\n   500\\t  // smoothly (\\\"entirely older than the smooth band's coverage\\\", with the\\n   501\\t  // newest-member tie-breaker subsumed by the retreat above). Newest-first.\\n   502\\t  const chunkCandidates = fullyBandedChunks\\n   503\\t    .filter((chunk) => liveMembersOf(chunk).every((turn) => !smoothTurnIds.has(turn.turnId)))\\n   504\\t    .reverse();\\n   505\\t\\n   506\\t  // Detailed fill: ≤ inclusion, crossing chunk stops the band, one oversized\\n   507\\t  // chunk still represents on an empty band (rule 3's \\\"same fill rule\\\").\\n   508\\t  function fillChunkBand(\\n   509\\t    candidates: readonly SelectionChunk[],\\n   510\\t    bandBudget: number,\\n   511\\t    band: \\\"detailed\\\" | \\\"brief\\\",\\n   512\\t    lonerException: boolean,\\n   513\\t  ): { included: ArrangementEntry[]; rest: SelectionChunk[] } {\\n   514\\t    const included: ArrangementEntry[] = [];\\n   515\\t    let sum = 0;\\n   516\\t    for (let i = 0; i < candidates.length; i += 1) {\\n   517\\t      const entry = buildChunkEntry(candidates[i] as SelectionChunk, band);\\n   518\\t      if (sum + entry.tokens <= bandBudget) {\\n   519\\t        included.push(entry);\\n   520\\t        sum += entry.tokens;\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"artifactsRead\\\":[\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\\\"],\\\"reviewScopeSummary\\\":\\\"Required docs are read. Implementation review is focused on compact selection/render/snapshot behavior, receipt metadata, production-path fakes, and mapped tests/gates.\\\",\\\"priorFindingStatuses\\\":[],\\\"newFindings\\\":[],\\\"openFindings\\\":[],\\\"requirementCoverage\\\":{\\\"verified\\\":[],\\\"unverified\\\":[\\\"AC-2.1\\\",\\\"AC-2.2\\\",\\\"AC-2.3\\\",\\\"AC-2.4\\\",\\\"AC-2.5\\\",\\\"AC-2.6\\\",\\\"AC-2.7\\\",\\\"AC-2.9\\\",\\\"AC-2.10\\\",\\\"AC-1.4\\\",\\\"AC-1.6\\\",\\\"TC-1.3\\\",\\\"TC-1.5\\\",\\\"TC-2.1\\\",\\\"TC-2.2\\\",\\\"TC-2.3\\\",\\\"TC-2.4\\\",\\\"TC-2.6\\\",\\\"TC-2.7\\\"]},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[],\\\"productionPathFindings\\\":[],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"block\\\",\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\",\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"additionalObservations\\\":[]}\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:86:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_42\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json | sed -n '1,260p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t{\\\"command\\\":\\\"story-implement\\\",\\\"version\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\\"result\\\":{\\\"resultId\\\":\\\"b5a6090d-9726-46c7-acec-503f3bfb46db\\\",\\\"provider\\\":\\\"claude-code\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-fable-5\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"story_implementor\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\\\",\\\"continuation\\\":{\\\"provider\\\":\\\"claude-code\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\\\",\\\"storyId\\\":\\\"02-smart-compact\\\"},\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\\"story\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"02-smart-compact\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Story 2: Smart Compact\\\"},\\\"planSummary\\\":\\\"Built compact inside-out per the story's build strategy: (1) render.ts gained the degrade ladders (smooth/detailed/brief resolvers), gap entries as last rung, §subject keys, [degraded: …]/[inter-turn note] markers, and band assembly; (2) select.ts is new — readSelectionInputs (record/forms reads with the canonical-corruption check in the reads, pre-transaction) plus the pure selectArrangement walk implementing rules 1–6 with pinned tie-breakers (≤ inclusion, newest-first, turn-boundary snap, straggler attachment, coverage edge); (3) snapshot.ts gained replaceViewSnapshot — one BEGIN IMMEDIATE doing delete-cascade, header+band insert, and boundary reset; (4) index.ts compact assembles validate → [sweep absent] → read → select → render → injection point → atomic replace → CompactReceipt with sweep: \\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\". Entry costs are tokens of the exact rendered entry text (one renderer, no drift). Two ambiguities surfaced during golden derivation and were pinned with code rationale: (a) turns whose chunk straddles the tail or is open are smooth-obligate and always render (AC-2.4's sanctioned over-bound indivisible-entry case — the alternative silently drops spans, violating TC-2.3); (b) a budget stop splitting a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk so it represents whole; (c) the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4's coverage edge is the documented exclusion path). Goldens G1–G4 were hand-derived from the rules against the fixture's deterministic token costs, verified against the pure walk, committed as JSON, and pinned in the immutability manifest.\\\",\\\"changedFiles\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"NEW: selection inputs read with pre-transaction corruption detection (CanonicalCorruptionError) + pure six-rule arrangement walk with coverage edge\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Band-entry side: degrade-ladder resolvers per band, gap entries, §keys, degraded/inter-turn-note markers, excerpt lines, band text assembly\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"replaceViewSnapshot: atomic BEGIN IMMEDIATE delete-cascade/insert/boundary-reset (AC-2.6)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"compact real: profile/params validation as caller errors, corruption abort, compact-write injection point, receipt with sweep \\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\"; stub removed\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Extracted profileViolation so construction (throw) and compact (caller-error result) share one rule set\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/shared/view.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"CompactReceipt.sweep gains the \\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\" literal (Story 3 debt comment referencing this story file); new ViewCompactParams (nested-partial params for field-wise band overrides, AC-2.2)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/shared/errors.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Two additive caller-error codes: unknown_profile, invalid_view_config (no new classes)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/sdk.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"ThreadViewSurface.compact params type → ViewCompactParams; type re-exported\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"test/red-manifest.json\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Re-recorded: amended view-pull.test.ts, new test files, and the five golden JSONs pinned for immutability\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"test/goldens/README.md\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Golden inventory, immutability rule, GOLDEN_DUMP=1 regeneration instructions\\\"}],\\\"tests\\\":{\\\"added\\\":[\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 rejections named (105 sum, non-positive bound, unknown profile), thread unchanged by read-back\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 built-in profile compact, bound+mix in receipt, sweep literal 'absent'\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1/AC-2.2 field-wise param override over a named profile, receipt profile null\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.2 actuals near shares with whole-entry deviations, zero provider calls, record hash unchanged\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.6 §chunk keys in brief/detailed, §turn keys in smooth\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk coverage edge: covered_from=13, exclusion reported, no phantom gaps\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk restart: fresh SDK pulls byte-identical snapshot\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.4 crash injection at compact-write: prior view serves, rerun lands, no partial rows\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.3 degraded compact: pending rendering → excerpt, failed brief summary → detailed-truncated, c2 gap with reason, full accounting, zero provider calls\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.5 completion leg: status view-health live (degraded=2, gaps=1, builtAt)\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 canonical corruption → state_corruption naming open turns, prior view serves, record unchanged\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 control: derived-only damage compacts\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.3 banded-subject edit + drain → band bytes hash-identical, rebuilt summary in record only\\\",\\\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.5 tail delete vanishes; banded delete leaves snapshot; status reflects record change\\\",\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G1 proportions vs committed JSON\\\",\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2a exact-fill inclusion (≤ rule)\\\",\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2b one-under exclusion, band stops\\\",\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G3 oversized loner represents alone\\\",\\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G4 straggler rides following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail\\\"],\\\"modified\\\":[\\\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: sanctioned amendment — compact's not-implemented leg removed (operation is real); sweep/materialize stub assertions kept\\\"],\\\"removed\\\":[],\\\"totalAfterStory\\\":263,\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\":20},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm run green-verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm run verify-all\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"}],\\\"selfReview\\\":{\\\"passesRun\\\":0,\\\"findingsFixed\\\":[\\\"Initial literal reading of rules 2–4 silently dropped spans when the smooth budget stopped mid-chunk or a chunk straddled the tail (found by dumping the fixture: t4/t5 vanished under 25/25/25/25) — fixed with smooth-obligate always-include + partial-chunk retreat, both grounded in AC-2.4's indivisible-entry over-bound allowance and AC-2.5's never-omit\\\",\\\"Compact-point walk had a malformed never-reached-budget branch — rewritten as explicit crossing detection\\\",\\\"Referential corruption check wrongly compared chunk members against live turns only — tombstoned turns are legitimate reference targets, now checked against all turn rows\\\",\\\"receipt.profile initially named the base profile even when params overrode it — corrected to null whenever explicit params are present (tech design §Storage: 'null when explicit params')\\\",\\\"Pinned Partial<ViewProfile> params type could not express the single-band override AC-2.2 itself requires — deepened to ViewCompactParams (nested partial)\\\"],\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\":[\\\"Golden authoring note: arrangements were hand-derived from the design rules using the fixture's deterministic token costs (dumped via a throwaway script, deleted), then the pure walk was checked against the hand derivation before committing — the goldens encode the rules, with regeneration instructions gated on the deviation process\\\",\\\"view-pull.test.ts's skeleton test asserted compact returns not_implemented; amended under the established Epic 02 sanctioned-amendment precedent (cc304bb) and the manifest re-recorded\\\"]},\\\"openQuestions\\\":[\\\"Default base profile for a bare compact({}) is pinned to 'continuation' (first built-in, the epic's primary PI-continuation user); the design names no default — confirm or change the pin before the CLI (Story 5 surface) exposes it\\\"],\\\"specDeviations\\\":[\\\"Pinned interpretation (not a behavior change to any stated rule): banded turns with no available chunk representation (chunk open or straddling the tail) always render in the smooth band even past its share — justified by AC-2.4's 'above it (an indivisible turn… included by the selection rules)' and required by AC-2.5/TC-2.3's no-silent-absence; documented in select.ts\\\",\\\"Pinned interpretation: a budget stop that splits a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk (a chunk represents all of its members or none) — closes the straddle hole rule 3's 'entirely older' would otherwise leave\\\",\\\"Pinned interpretation: the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4 states the coverage edge, not 'same fill rule') — without this, the oldest chunk could never fall outside the window and the coverage-edge AC would be untestable\\\",\\\"compact opts params type is ViewCompactParams (nested partial) rather than the sketched Partial<ViewProfile> — AC-2.2's field-wise band override is inexpressible in the sketched type\\\",\\\"Additive vocabulary: ErrorCode gains unknown_profile and invalid_view_config (caller_error class; no new classes per the error contract); CompactReceipt.sweep gains the 'absent' literal this story (Story 3 flips it, comment references this story file)\\\"],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Run story verification; on acceptance proceed to Story 3 (sweep) — its gate requires confirming the Epic 02 requeue patch and the persisted terminal-failure reason classes (FC-0.4 already proves the fixture side), and it flips the receipt's sweep field from the 'absent' literal to SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }\\\"},\\\"